        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Bisecting a line AB requires drawing arcs from points A and B with the same radius, intersecting above and below the line, then joining the intersection points. <b>Drawing a perpendicular from the midpoint</b> is unnecessary as the bisector is already perpendicular.</p>",
